  "reviewer_notes": "The paper fits three linear-regression energy base lines (E = mP + b), one per fertilizer reference (15-15-15, 13-26-6, 17-6-18-2), each with its own coefficients and R²; these are recorded as three models (M1–M3). The Efficiency Index Base 100 is recorded as a fourth model (M4, composite index). The consumption index (kWh/TM, theoretical vs actual) and CUSUM are mentioned but not detailed enough to model separately. The dependent variable is 'Energy (kWh/day)'; the paper repeatedly frames the managed energy as natural gas, so energy_vector is coded 'natural gas' by inference despite the kWh/day unit (there is a possible unit/vector ambiguity). The plant-level energy saving potentials (16.1% good operational practices, 25.6% production planning) derive from the combined baseline/goal-line analysis; they are attributed to M1 (the 15-15-15 base product) with support_class 'requires inference' rather than duplicated across all models. Baseline period taken as 2015 from the abstract; control charts span dic-14 to dic-15.",
